Terminology:
============

We use "head" to mean the tip of the branch used for daily development
(in our case, the "master" branch).

We use "branch" to mean the release branch being worked on.

Below "AI" means "Action Item", these are the various steps needed to
complete each task.

checklist:
==========

   * filename:
     ~~~~~~~~~
        var/checklists/gdb-<BRANCH_VERSION>.yaml
        (Eg: var/checklists/gdb-7.7.yaml).

        Should be automatically created by the release script
        as soon as the current version gets bumped.

   * format:
     ~~~~~~~

       - branch-creation:
           - AI
           - AI
           (etc)
       - gdb-<version>-release:
           - AI
           (etc)

     The reason for using "nested series entry indicator" it to allow us
     to preserve the order when dumping the yaml file after each AI gets
     completed.  This makes it easier to track where we're at, what's
     been done, and what still remains to be done.

var/releases.yaml
=================

   * To create a new branch:
     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

       1. Update the "current-branch:" value.
       2. Create a section whose name is the new "current-branch:" value.
          Follow the same pattern as previous branches.

   * To create a new release (or pre-release):
     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

     Just add a "do_release: <version-number>" entry at the end of
     the corresponding release block in var/releases.yaml.

     TIP: Do not delete old ones, as they are a great track record
     of the releases created off that branch.
